@startuml AD-1
!include _style.iuml
title AD-1 (System level) — Charge a vehicle with the Driver App\nTrigger: Driver arrives at a station found in the app (UC-CHG-01) · Use cases: UC-CHG-02, 03, 04, UC-INT-03

|«person»\nDriver|
start
:Plug in, scan connector QR code\nand choose billing mode and limit;
|«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
:Check connector status\nand vehicle compatibility;
if ( ) then ([BR-P38: busy, faulted, offline,\nreserved by another Driver\nor incompatible])
  :Refuse with reason and\nnearby available connectors;
  stop
else ([Available, or Reserved by\nthis Driver, and compatible])
endif
|«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
:Check Charging Credit\nagainst start minimum;
while ( ) is ([BR-P18: credit < start minimum])
  |«person»\nDriver|
  if ( ) then ([Driver cancels])
    stop
  else ([Driver tops up])
    :Top Up Charging Credit ⋔;
  endif
  |«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
endwhile ([credit ≥ start minimum])
if ( ) then ([BR-P29: Driver holds a reservation\non this connector])
  :Reservation\n&#91;fulfilled&#93;]
else ([else])
endif
if ( ) then ([BR-P18: limit costs more than the\ncredit at the highest tariff of the day])
  :Refuse with the largest affordable\nlimit (Driver may start again with it);
  stop
else ([affordable])
endif
:Create start request and hold\nthe limit's cost from credit;
:ChargingSession\n&#91;pending&#93;]
note right
  For an app start, pending and failed
  are held on the start request
  (driver_charge_intents); the sessions
  row is created in active when the
  Charge Point reports the start.
end note
:Send start request>
|«external system»\nCharge Point|
if ( ) then ([start rejected])
  |«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
  :Refuse the start, keep no\nhold and notify Driver;
  stop
elseif ( ) then ([no reply within 30 s])
  |«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
  :Mark start outcome unknown, credit\nstays held until the Operator\nfences the connector (WF-03);
  stop
elseif ( ) then ([accepted, but no start\nwithin 120 s])
  |«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
  :Close start request without\ncharge, release hold, notify Driver;
  :ChargingSession\n&#91;failed&#93;]
  stop
else ([start accepted\nand started])
  |«external system»\nCharge Point|
  :Lock connector and\nstart energy delivery;
endif
|«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
:ChargingSession\n&#91;active&#93;]
while ( ) is ([BR-P19: no stop condition])
  |«external system»\nCharge Point|
  :Send meter reading>
  |«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
  :Update energy, cost and\ncredit left; push progress;
  |«person»\nDriver|
  :View battery level, energy,\ntime and running cost;
  |«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
endwhile ([stop condition met])
if ( ) then ([BR-P01, P19: Driver stops, limit reached\nor credit at cutoff reserve])
  if ( ) then ([Driver chose to stop])
    |«person»\nDriver|
    :Tap Stop;
  else ([else])
  endif
  |«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
  :Send stop request>
  :ChargingSession\n&#91;stopping&#93;]
else ([vehicle battery full])
endif
|«external system»\nCharge Point|
:Stop delivery, unlock connector\nand send final meter reading>
|«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
:ChargingSession\n&#91;closed&#93;]
:ChargingSession\n&#91;reconciled&#93;]
:Price per tariff period and\ndebit cost from Charging Credit;
:CreditTransaction\n&#91;session_debit&#93;]
if ( ) then ([BR-P20: cost > credit balance:\nnew starts blocked\nuntil top-up])
  :CreditAccount\n&#91;in_shortfall&#93;]
else ([else])
endif
fork
  :Count the session once in\nthe revenue report (BR-P46);
fork again
  :Award loyalty points;
  :LoyaltyTransaction\n&#91;earn&#93;]
end fork
:Send charging statement;
|«person»\nDriver|
:View statement and\nunplug the connector;
stop
@enduml
